    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36564" root="كبر" body-key="k">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كبّر</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تكَبِيرٌ</span>, <i>He made</i> a thing <i>great.</i>
(K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He magnified,</i> or <i>honoured;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَظَّمَ</span>.
(S) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also, inf. n. as above, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِبَّارٌ</span>, (Sgh,
K,) which latter is of the dial. of Belhárith Ibn-Kaab and many of the people of El-Yemen,
(Sgh,) <i>He said</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَللّٰهُ أَكْبَر</span>. (K.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَكْبَرُ</span>,
below.

